TEXT 96 240 Left 2 ;This example shows the load macro model from ltspice.lib\nIf k = 2 the load behaves like a normal constpowerload\nIf k = 1 the load behaves like a constcurrentload\nIf k = 0 the load behaves like a constimpedanceload
TEXT -184 344 Left 2 ;Change the p and q values \nWhat is if p = 200e6
TEXT -112 24 Left 2 !.step param vpar list 0.9 1 1.1
TEXT 24 24 Left 2 !.param kpar=2
TEXT 24 32 Left 2 !.param vpar=1
TEXT -24 344 Left 2 ;Result:\n \nYou see that the biggest power changes ( on altering the voltage V1 ) are with\nthe constimpedanceload due to the quadratic relation V to P\nThe constcurrentload has lower powerchanges due to the only linear relation V to P\nThe constpowerload has no powerchange at all at different voltage levels !!
TEXT -24 -88 Left 5 ;Example with a special load element \nWith the parameter k you can alter the behaviour of the model
TEXT -112 0 Left 2 !.param tdv=1 tdt=1 fn1=50 omega_n={2*pi*fn1}
